UID: NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER-GAP-IDENTITY-HAS-NO-CARRIER
TITLE: Identity has no carrier
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
WIDGET: prose
STATEMENT: >>>
Every rule about who may do something — sign a contract, raise authorship, accept a decision, groom, delete — needs to know who is acting. The three things that would tell it (the hook layer's actor slot — the field in a handler's payload that would say who is acting; the table mapping keys to human-or-agent; and the guard that reads it) are unbuilt and nobody owns them. Meanwhile about ten rulings, and the acceptance flow itself, already carry human authority under an agent's key.

Nodes it touches: [LINK: MECH-HOOK-MIDDLEWARE-INTERFACE], [LINK: DEC-FP-ACCEPT-AUTHORITY], [LINK: DEC-NO-DELETES-YET] and [LINK: SLICE-HOOK-LAYER].
